    <briefdescription>
<para>Abstract base class for sound file encoding. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This class allows users to write audio file formats not natively supported by SFML, and thus extend the set of supported writable audio formats.</para>
<para>A valid sound file writer must override the open and write functions, as well as providing a static check function; the latter is used by SFML to find a suitable writer for a given filename.</para>
<para>To register a new writer, use the <computeroutput><ref refid="classsf_1_1SoundFileFactory_1a3a59140e6ccf1f252f721b790eddd661" kindref="member">sf::SoundFileFactory::registerWriter</ref></computeroutput> template function.</para>
<para>Usage example: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="keyword">class<sp/></highlight><highlight class="normal">MySoundFileWriter<sp/>:<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">public</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>sf::SoundFileWriter</highlight></codeline>
